EVERY TIME
1.start Docker
2.minikube start
3.kubectl get pods
4.minikube service my-cv AND LEAVE IT RUNNING

USEFUL
minikube stop      # shut the cluster down cleanly (keeps your work)
minikube start     # bring it back
minikube delete    # wipe the whole cluster and start from scratch

WHEN I CHANGE SOMETHING IN DEPLOYMENT
kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml
kubectl get pods

IF I CHANGE SOMETHING IN THE HTML (I DO VERSION2) 
My running pods don’t see the change. The HTML is baked into the image, so I have to build a new image and tell Kubernetes to use it.
Kubernetes then does a rolling update. It starts new pods with v2, waits until they’re ready, and removes the old v1 pods one at a time, so the site never goes down.
minikube image build -t mycv:v2 ./app
Change the image line in deployment.yaml: image: mycv:v2
kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml
kubectl get pods